---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Temple Court",
  servesCuisine: ["American", "Contemporary"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-917-728-4685",
  url: "https://www.templecourtnyc.com",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "5 Beekman St",
    addressLocality: "New York",
    addressRegion: "NY",
    postalCode: "10038",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Tom Colicchio's restaurant inside The Beekman hotel's nine-story Victorian atrium in the Financial District — classic American cooking with a seasonal touch.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Temple Court Menu Guide — Beekman Hotel, Prices, Picks"
  description="Independent guide to Temple Court at The Beekman: Tom Colicchio's atrium dining room, reported prices, signature dishes, the Bar Room, and visiting tips. Prices reported as of October 2026."
  path="/temple-court-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/temple-court.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/temple-court.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a grand Victorian hotel atrium dining room with a skylight — an artist's interpretation, not the actual Temple Court"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Financial District · The Beekman
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Temple Court — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Step into The Beekman hotel at 5 Beekman Street and the city falls away: a nine-story
      Victorian atrium rises overhead, capped by a pyramidal skylight. In this setting, Tom
      Colicchio serves the old-and-new American classics he built his name on — seasonal,
      precise, and unmistakably his. (The room opened as Fowler &amp; Wells in 2016 and took the
      Temple Court name in 2017.) Below is our independent walkthrough of the menu, reported
      prices, and how to plan the visit. Everything is written in our own words; prices are
      reported figures, not a copy of the restaurant's menu.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">5 Beekman St, New York, NY 10038 (inside The Beekman, FiDi)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Tom Colicchio</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Contemporary American — classics reimagined, seasonal</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Fine dining — a la carte bands reported below; 3-course Restaurant Week $60 (summer 2026)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Reported: breakfast &amp; lunch daily 7am–3pm; dinner Mon &amp; Sun 5:30–9:30pm, Tue–Sat 5:30–10pm</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+1 (917) 728-4685</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>What the menu looks like</h2>
      <p>
        Temple Court runs a full-day operation — breakfast, lunch, weekend brunch, and dinner —
        with dinner as the main event: an a la carte menu of first courses, mains and desserts,
        plus a five-course tasting menu. Published figures from past seasons put <strong>first
        courses roughly in the mid-$20s and mains from the high $30s into the $70s</strong>, but the
        menu changes regularly with the market, so treat those bands as a guide and confirm current
        prices when you book. One solid recent data point: the restaurant's <strong>Summer 2026
        Restaurant Week menu offered three courses for $60</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Signature dishes to know</h2>
      <p>
        These are the dishes that define the room — reported on the restaurant's seasonal menus and
        in diners' accounts. Exact preparations change with the market; the ideas recur.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Notes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Tomato tarte tatin</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Signature starter</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Chestnut agnolotti</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Signature pasta</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Foie graffle (foie gras waffle)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Signature starter</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Skate meunière</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Classic main</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Smoked wagyu brisket</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Signature main</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Dry-aged prime NY strip with roasted sunchokes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Steakhouse anchor</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Chilled corn bisque</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Seasonal starter</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Braised lamb shoulder</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Seasonal main</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Spanish octopus</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Seasonal main</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Corn tres leches</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">Signature dessert</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Our take: the tomato tarte tatin and the corn tres leches are the two dishes most associated
        with this kitchen — if they're on the menu the night you visit, don't overthink it.
      </p>

      <h2>The Bar Room</h2>
      <p>
        Adjacent to the dining room, The Bar Room sits directly in the atrium — sixteen antique brass
        and emerald stools, velvet sofas, live jazz on some nights, and a menu of classic cocktails
        with bar snacks (reported items have included clams casino, steak tartare, and a blueberry
        millefeuille). If the dining room feels like a commitment, the Bar Room is the lower-key way
        to drink in the architecture. Bar snack prices were not verifiable from public sources at the
        time of writing — ask for the current menu at the bar.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To start:</strong> the tomato tarte tatin — it's the dish the room is known for.</li>
        <li><strong>The main:</strong> skate meunière or the dry-aged strip, depending on appetite.</li>
        <li><strong>Dessert:</strong> corn tres leches — Colicchio's sweet signature.</li>
        <li><strong>The alternative:</strong> a cocktail and bar snacks in the Bar Room, gazing up nine stories. Sometimes that's the better evening.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book dinner ahead</strong> — the atrium is a destination and weekend tables go first.</li>
        <li><strong>Daytime is a secret.</strong> Breakfast and lunch in the atrium (reported daily 7am–3pm) are calmer, cheaper ways to see the room.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the tasting menu.</strong> The five-course option has been offered historically; confirm availability and price when reserving, as we could not verify current figures.</li>
        <li><strong>FiDi at night is quiet</strong> — plan your ride home; the subway is close but the streets empty out early.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Prices above are <strong>reported as of October 2026</strong>. Temple Court's menu changes
        with the seasons and the market, and published a la carte figures vary across sources — the
        bands given here come from past published menus and should be treated as a guide. The $60
        three-course figure is from the restaurant's Summer 2026 Restaurant Week menu. Always verify
        current prices with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
